            note: 'Heindel had heard Steiner in Germany, as the descent on this page records. Secondary accounts of the Rosicrucian Fellowship’s emblem give seven red roses on a white cross before a radiant five-pointed star on blue. The likeness to Steiner’s seven roses is plain. But no document records that the emblem was taken from him, and its first dated use was not found.',
